Here is the commit message:
Fix statfs_x bug when using modules

This fixes a bug introduced in commit ba5744c. We need to track whether
the actual file system implements the high-level statfs_x callback or
not. Checking if f->op.statfs_x exists is not sufficient in case
modules are used.

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by an insufficient check for the existence of the high-level `statfs_x` callback in file systems that use modules. The original implementation only checked if `f->fs->op.statfs_x` existed, which did not account for scenarios where the actual file system might not implement this callback, leading to incorrect behavior when modules were involved.

Here is the patch:
 	int nullpath_ok;
